      "message": "This changes the behavior below: now if there is no socket left for this key, it will notify that all sockets were destroyed on the network; which may not be true if there are several sockets on the network (for tethered interfaces).\n\nThis should either check if any socket is active on the network, or notify that all sockets were destroyed for the SocketKey (but not the whole Network)",
